%description:

Tcp.increasedIWEnabled:on -- the deprecated parameter selects the window of RFC 3390.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "deprecated: the same as initialWindow = "rfc3390" (RFC 3390)".

The classes: off (false, the default), on (true: initialWindow "rfc3390") and conflict (true
with initialWindow "rfc6928": an error). The code: TcpConnection::configureStateVariables(). This test separates "on" from "off".

Host under test: host1, with initialWindow "rfc2001", which sends 30000 bytes. Observation: level 1, the data segments that host1 sends before the first ACK of data comes
back: the links have a delay of 10 ms, so the round trip is 40 ms, and a full-sized segment
has 1448 bytes. The first
flight is three segments, as with "rfc3390".

%# parameter: Tcp.increasedIWEnabled
%# class: on
%# value: true
%# key: *.host1.tcp.increasedIWEnabled
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpIncreasedIWEnabledOn")
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
             .capture("isn", "tcp.sequenceNo")
             .describe("the SYN of host1")
             .within(0.5))
        .meanwhile(anyNumberOfTimes(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
                                        .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == false && pk.dataLength > tcp.headerLength")
                                        .captureCount("flight")
                                        .describe("each data segment of host1")
                                        .within(2.0)))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetReceivedFromLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == false && tcp.ackBit == true && tcp.ackNo > {isn} + 1")
             .first()
                  .assertPacket("{flight} == 3")
             .describe("the first ACK of data, after 3 data segments")
             .within(1.0));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpIncreasedIWEnabledOn compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.increasedIWEnabled = true    # the parameter under test
*.host1.tcp.initialWindow = "rfc2001"
*.linkDelay = 10ms
*.host1.app[0].sendBytes = 30000B
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpIncreasedIWEnabledOn: PASS
